@0xCardiE  Hi! Thanks for working on this issue. I appreciate the effort you put into creating comprehensive error handling.

However, I think we might be over-engineering the solution here. The core issue is that Drizzle wraps PostgreSQL errors and only shows the SQL query in the error message, hiding the actual error in the cause property.

  A simpler fix would be to:
  1. Add a basic connection test at the start of migrations
  2. Extract the actual error from the cause property when catching errors

  Here's what works well:

  // In runPluginMigrations
  ```
  try {
    await db.execute(sql.raw('SELECT 1'));
    logger.debug('[CUSTOM MIGRATOR] Database connection verified');
  } catch (error) {
    let errorMessage = 'Unknown error';
    if (error instanceof Error && 'cause' in error && error.cause) {
      errorMessage = (error.cause as Error).message;
    } else if (error instanceof Error) {
      errorMessage = error.message;
    }
    logger.error(`[CUSTOM MIGRATOR] Database connection failed: ${errorMessage}`);
    throw new Error(`Database connection failed: ${errorMessage}`);
  }
```
  This gives us clean error messages like Database connection failed: getaddrinfo ENOTFOUND localhost without needing a separate error handler class.

